{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvxJmx8xD1VmcxHHtAS2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0197yxTR7rjhBznVSztjre2B","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; cp paper.tex paper.pre_citeweave.tex; python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('paper.tex',encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1,a[:50]; s=s.replace(a,b)\n\nrep(r\"\\section{Related Work}\\label{sec:related}\n\\paragraph{Conditional validity.}\",\nr\"\"\"\\section{Related Work}\\label{sec:related}\n\\paragraph{Foundations and classification scores.}\nSplit (inductive) conformal prediction trades the full-conformal refit for a held-out calibration set and retains finite-sample marginal coverage under exchangeability \\citep{Vovk2005Algorithmic,Lei2018Distribution}; Mondrian conformal prediction applies the same rank argument within the cells of a partition and is treated in the same monograph \\citep{Vovk2005Algorithmic}. For classifiers, the least-ambiguous-set construction thresholds the softmax mass of each label \\citep{Sadinle2019Least}, adaptive prediction sets accumulate sorted probability mass with randomisation \\citep{Romano2020Classification}, and a regularised variant penalises large ranks to shrink sets on many-class problems \\citep{Angelopoulos2020Uncertainty}. These score families are the comparators of Section~\\ref{sec:method}.\n\n\\paragraph{Conditional validity.}\"\"\")\n\nrep(r\"Applied and tutorial treatments of conformal classifiers appear in clinical imaging, histopathology, pattern recognition and software-tutorial venues \\citep{Cina2026QuantifyingCC,Gelvez2025ConformalPF,Rueda2007ProgressIP,Löfström2022TutorialFU}.\",\nr\"Applied treatments of conformal classifiers appear in clinical imaging and histopathology \\citep{Cina2026QuantifyingCC,Gelvez2025ConformalPF}.\")\n\nrep(r\"\"\"\\paragraph{Positioning.}\nOur contribution\"\"\",\nr\"\"\"\\paragraph{Distribution shift.}\nExchangeability fails under covariate shift, where test inputs follow a different density from calibration inputs. If the density ratio is known, reweighting the calibration scores by it and giving the test point its own weight restores marginal coverage \\citep{Tibshirani2019Conformal}; the ratio can be estimated with a probabilistic classifier that separates calibration from test inputs, at the cost of an approximate guarantee. Our gated step follows this recipe with an estimated ratio and an explicit fallback to the unweighted procedure.\n\n\\paragraph{Positioning.}\nOur contribution\"\"\")\n\nrep(r\"Compositional-data analysis in the sense of log-ratio geometry motivates the framing (outputs live on the simplex)\",\nr\"Compositional-data analysis in the sense of log-ratio geometry \\citep{Aitchison1982Statistical} motivates the framing (outputs live on the simplex)\")\n\nrep(r\"The evaluator scores four standard split-conformal baselines on identical data with the same loss: LAC (threshold on $1-p_y$), APS (randomised cumulative-mass score), RAPS (APS with a rank penalty,\",\nr\"The evaluator scores four standard split-conformal baselines on identical data with the same loss, drawn from the score families of Section~\\ref{sec:related}: LAC \\citep{Sadinle2019Least} (threshold on $1-p_y$), APS \\citep{Romano2020Classification} (randomised cumulative-mass score), RAPS \\citep{Angelopoulos2020Uncertainty} (APS with a rank penalty,\")\n\nrep(r\"and class-wise LAC. Uncalibrated\",\nr\"and class-wise LAC (LAC calibrated separately per label, in the spirit of the class-conditional methods cited above). The exact implementations are those in the evaluator source, not re-derived from the cited papers. Uncalibrated\")\n\nrep(r\"and coverage conditional on the calibration set follows a $\\mathrm{Beta}(k,n+1-k)$ law. Applying\",\nr\"and coverage conditional on the calibration set follows a $\\mathrm{Beta}(k,n+1-k)$ law \\citep{Vovk2005Algorithmic,Lei2018Distribution}. Applying\")\nrep(r\"(Mondrian calibration); with $G$ equal\",r\"(Mondrian calibration, \\citealt{Vovk2005Algorithmic}); with $G$ equal\")\nrep(r\"These are textbook statements and we do not claim them as new.\",r\"These are textbook statements \\citep{Vovk2005Algorithmic} and we do not claim them as new.\")\n\nrep(r\"placing the test point's weight at $+\\infty$ in the weighted empirical distribution of calibration scores restores marginal coverage;\",\nr\"placing the test point's weight at $+\\infty$ in the weighted empirical distribution of calibration scores restores marginal coverage \\citep{Tibshirani2019Conformal};\")\n\nrep(r\"; several standard references on split-conformal theory, covariate-shift weighting and compositional data analysis are not in the retrieved bibliography and are therefore stated as background without citation.\",\nr\". Citations to the split/Mondrian, score-function, covariate-shift and compositional-data sources (Section~\\ref{sec:related}) support background statements only; the retrieval metadata record titles, venues and years, and the implementation details of the baselines and of the studied procedure come from the evaluator and candidate sources, not from those papers.\")\nopen('paper.tex','w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nE\ngrep -n 'label{sec:method}' paper.tex; grep -n 'Section~\\\\ref{sec:method}' paper.tex | head -3"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":228,"cache_read_input_tokens":78247,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":228},"output_tokens":36,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6bfae6f9-e277-47df-a508-24d3af227d39","uuid":"8670dd4b-1d88-45fe-bc02-25444f958e00","timestamp":"2026-11-11T10:06:51.019Z","request_id":"r